cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "VLUN: a provenance-preserving smart-contract security reasoning dataset"
version: 2.2
date-released: 2026-10-07
repository-code: "https://github.com/Nimvex1/vlun-data"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - smart contracts
  - vulnerability detection
  - security auditing
  - software engineering
  - machine learning
  - blockchain
authors:
  - name: "Code4rena competitive-audit participants"
    role: "finding authors (original audit sources)"
  - name: "Professional audit firms and contest platforms"
    role: "finding authors (see NOTICE.md and Vbeta ingestion reports)"
abstract: >
  A provenance-preserving corpus of smart-contract security findings across
  Solidity, Rust, Move, Cairo, Circom, Noir, Leo, TypeScript, Go, Vyper and
  Clarity. Every record traces to a public artefact and every claim carries
  its evidence type. Governing rule: truth over scale; unknown is a counted
  outcome. Data layers are CC BY 4.0; pipeline scripts are MIT; third-party
  source is not licensed here at all (see NOTICE.md).
preferred-citation:
  type: dataset
  title: "VLUN: a provenance-preserving smart-contract security reasoning dataset"
  version: 2.2
  repository-code: "https://github.com/Nimvex1/vlun-data"
